  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 159 AM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will continue to dominate the regional\nweather, though will shift from the Mid-South to High Plains and\nthen back again over the next several days. Heat will be a factor\nin the weather as this ridge remains stout. Closer to the Gulf\nCoast, however, we will see increasing rain chances associated\nwith an easterly wave bring a surge of deeper moisture and eroding\nthe edge of the ridge. Rain chances may nudge back to the south\nwhen the ridge centers over the High Plains over the weekend, but\nmost days even a stray shower or storm could occur in northern\nparts of our CWA. Locally heavy rainfall with deep tropical\nmoisture in place will be a possible concern. And wherever rain\ndelays until afternoon hours, heat index values will still\napproach the 105+ range each day. Expect additional Heat Advisory\nheadlines for at least parts of the area into next week. /NF/",
